│ 1. Bug Location and Intended Behavior                              │
│                                                                    │
│  • Bug Location 1:                                                 │
│    File: django/db/backends/base/schema.py                         │
│    Class: BaseDatabaseSchemaEditor                                 │
│    Method: _delete_composed_index                                  │
│    Intended Behavior:                                              │
│    The method should delete the index only if it is no longer      │
│    needed, respecting constraints like unique_together and         │
│    index_together. The current implementation raises a ValueError  │
│    when there are multiple constraints (e.g., unique_together and  │
│    index_together) on the same fields, which is incorrect. The bug │
│    is that the code assumes all constraints are active when        │
│    deleting indexes, but it should only delete the index if it is  │
│    not required by any constraints.                                │
│  • Bug Location 2:                                                 │
│    File: django/db/backends/base/schema.py                         │
│    Class: Schema                                                   │
│    Method: _delete_composed_index                                  │
│    Intended Behavior:                                              │
│    The method should handle the deletion of indexes while ensuring │
│    that constraints like unique_together are respected. The        │
│    current logic incorrectly counts constraints, leading to the    │
│    crash when index_together is used alongside unique_together on  │
│    the same fields.                                                │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                          Key Fixes Needed                          │
│                                                                    │
│ To resolve the issue, the _delete_composed_index method must be    │
│ modified to:                                                       │
│                                                                    │
│  1 Check for unique_together constraints and skip deleting the     │
│    index if it is part of a unique_together constraint.            │
│  2 Only delete the index if it is not required by any active       │
│    constraints (e.g., unique_together or index_together).          │
│                                                                    │
│ This ensures that the index is not deleted when it is still        │
│ needed, preventing the ValueError and allowing migrations to       │
│ proceed without crashing.                                          │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                    Summary of Required Actions                     │
│                                                                    │
│  • Fix the _delete_composed_index method in schema.py to handle    │
│    unique_together constraints.                                    │
│  • Ensure migrations do not attempt to delete indexes that are     │
│    part of unique_together or index_together constraints.          │
│                                                                    │
│ This approach preserves existing functionality while resolving the │
│ crash caused by conflicting constraints.                           │
