│ The _delete_composed_index method is responsible for deleting a    │
│ composed index (e.g., an index defined via index_together) in the  │
│ database schema. It checks the number of constraints (e.g.,        │
│ unique_together and index_together) that apply to the fields       │
│ involved and raises an error if there are multiple constraints.    │
│                                                                    │
