│                    Analysis of the Code Context                    │
│                                                                    │
│ 1. What does this part of the code do?                             │
│ The _delete_composed_index method is responsible for deleting a    │
│ composed index (e.g., an index defined via index_together) in the  │
│ database schema. It checks the number of constraints (e.g.,        │
│ unique_together and index_together) that apply to the fields       │
│ involved and raises an error if there are multiple constraints.    │
│                                                                    │
│ 2. What is the relationship between this part of the code and the  │
│ bug?                                                               │
│ The method is crashing when there are both unique_together and     │
│ index_together on the same fields. The error occurs because the    │
│ code assumes all constraints are active, but the intended behavior │
│ is to only delete the index if it is no longer needed (e.g., after │
│ unique_together is removed).                                       │
│                                                                    │
│ 3. Intended behavior of the code                                   │
│ The method should:                                                 │
│                                                                    │
│  • Skip deleting the index if it is part of a unique_together      │
│    constraint.                                                     │
│  • Only delete the index if it is not required by any active       │
│    constraints (e.g., unique_together or index_together).          │
│  • Avoid raising errors during index deletion when constraints are │
│    present.                                                        │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                      Bug Locations and Fixes                       │
│                                                                    │
│ Bug Location 1:                                                    │
