│ Intended Behavior:                                                 │
│ The method should check for unique_together constraints and skip   │
│ index deletion if the index is part of a unique_together           │
│ constraint. The current implementation does not account for this,  │
│ leading to the crash.                                              │
│                                                                    │
│ Bug Location 2:                                                    │
│ File: django/db/backends/base/schema.py                            │
│ Class: BaseDatabaseSchemaEditor                                    │
│ Method: _delete_composed_index                                     │
│ Intended Behavior:                                                 │
│ The method should only delete the index if it is not required by   │
│ any active constraints (e.g., unique_together or index_together).  │
│ The current logic incorrectly assumes all constraints are active,  │
│ causing the error.                                                 │
│                                                                    │
